ientation-dimension","title":"rem:hypersurface-orientation-dimension","tex":"\\begin{remark}\n\\label{rem:hypersurface-orientation-dimension}\n\\uses{prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal, def:smooth-orientation, def:induced-orientation}\n\nThe assumption $n\\ge1$ in Proposition \\ref{prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal} is necessary for this frame argument: a $0$-manifold has only the empty frame, while the induced orientation in a $1$-manifold can be the opposite ray determined by $dV_{\\widetilde g}(N_x)=\\pm1$.\n\\end{remark}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal","title":"prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation","title":"def:smooth-orientation","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-orientation","title":"def:induced-orientation","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}